// errors, DECLARED BY HAND. Every claim below was read off src/errors/errors.go and
// src/errors/wrap.go in the Go 1.27 toolchain.
//
// THE ALGEBRA. An error is the root of a TREE: err itself, then the errors its
// `Unwrap() error` or `Unwrap() []error` gives, depth first (Go 1.20). Over it:
//   Unwrap : error → 1 + error        one step down a chain: Unwrap's result, or
//                                      none when the type has no `Unwrap() error`
//                                      (a leaf, or a fork, whose Unwrap gives a list)
//   Is     : error × error → bool     ∃x in pre-order(err). x == target ∨ x.Is(target)
//   AsType : Π(E ∈ 𝒫(⟦error⟧)). error → 1 + E
//                                      the first x in pre-order(err) with x ∈ E (the type
//                                      assertion err.(E)), or whose As method claims it
//   New    : B* → error               a FRESH error: two calls with one text give two
//                                      values Is tells apart (errors.go: "Each call to New
//                                      returns a distinct error value even if the text is
//                                      identical"), so it is not pure — ADR 0010's pure
//                                      call may be duplicated.
//
// AsType IS A FUNCTION FROM SETS (spec/typevalues.md, ADR 0063): its type parameter
// occurs only in the result, so a call names it, `((errors.AsType strconv.NumError)
// e)`, and the application reduces at compile time to the instance, printed
// `errors.AsType[*strconv.NumError](e)`. Go's bound `[E error]` is membership in
// (subsets error), decided by the target's `implements`. Go returns (E, bool), its
// comma-ok, and E's zero value when the bool is false; `(comma-ok)` makes that the
// option, so the zero never reaches the program. The flag, not E's nil, is the
// truth: err.(E) holds of a typed nil inside a non-nil interface, and AsType then
// returns (nil, true).
//
// WHAT IS NOT DECLARED, named rather than hidden:
//   - As(err, target any) bool: AsType is the same search with no cell; As's target
//     is a pointer the host writes, a cell, and waits for a program that holds one.
//   - Join(errs ...error) error: a variadic over error whose result is nil when every
//     argument is; no program calls it yet.
//   - ErrUnsupported: a package variable no program compares against yet.
module go/errors {
    fn New(text ∈ bytestring) (error) { host expr "errors.New(${text})" import "errors" }
    fn Is(err ∈ error, target ∈ error) (Bool) {
        host expr "errors.Is(${err}, ${target})" import "errors"
    }
    fn Unwrap(err ∈ error) (Option(error)) { host expr "errors.Unwrap(${err})" import "errors" }
    fn AsType(E ⊆ error) {
        fn(err ∈ error) (Option(E)) {
            host expr "errors.AsType[${E}](${err})" import "errors" comma_ok
        }
    }
}
